          %h3#ChainCohomology Chain cohomology
          %p
            The probably most familiar kind of cohomology is that of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
            dual to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
          %p
            Using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+object"} spectrum object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "s" do
